\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Uber\uc2  Plays Down Driver Strike --- Company says New York City service not affected as union calls for 24-hour shutdown\b0\par\par\uc2 By Joseph Pisani \par \uc2 422 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Uber Technologies Inc\uc2 . said service in New York City wasn't affected Monday by a 24-hour strike set by a union that represents drivers.\par \par \uc2 The New York Taxi Workers Alliance organized the strike after a judge temporarily blocked wage increases that were supposed to go into effect Monday. The union and supporters of the striking \uc2 Uber\uc2  drivers asked New Yorkers not to use the ride-hailing app.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  said there were 3% more drivers online Monday morning than on an average Monday during the last half of the year. Ubers were available on the app Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Drivers were out there today doing critical work for New Yorkers, not listening to political chatter on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 ," \uc2 Uber\uc2  spokesman Josh Gold said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The New York Taxi Workers Alliance said the strike, which started just after midnight Monday, was to end at 11:59 p.m. The union also held a protest at \uc2 Uber\uc2 's New York offices on Monday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The dispute comes after \uc2 Uber\uc2  sued New York's Taxi & Limousine Commissionearlier this month for approving a pay increase for \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  drivers.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  said in the lawsuit that it would have to pay an additional $21 million to $23 million a month if the pay increases went into effect. That would force it to raise the average passenger fare in the city by 10%, the company said.\par \par \uc2 "Such a significant fare hike, right before the holidays, would irreparably damage \uc2 Uber\uc2 's reputation," the company said in its lawsuit, which asked for the pay increase to be temporarily stopped.\par \par \uc2 A judge agreed last week to temporarily stop pay raises.\par \par \uc2 About 30 people showed up at the protest in front of \uc2 Uber\uc2 's New York office. Drivers said \uc2 Uber\uc2  should drop the lawsuit. Some held signs that said, "\uc2 Uber\uc2  the Grinch stole our raise."\par \par \uc2 Abdul Quyyam, an \uc2 Uber\uc2  driver for seven years, said he came because the cost of groceries, gas and rent have all gone up. "We want our raise," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The bottom line is, \uc2 Uber\uc2  wants to pay nothing more to the drivers whose labor creates the company's profits," said \uc2 Bhairavi Desai\uc2 , the executive director of the New York Taxi Workers Alliance.\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez\uc2 , a Democrat from New York, said in a tweet that New Yorkers shouldn't use \uc2 Uber\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Turn off your \uc2 Uber\uc2  app," she said. "Use another service."\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020221220eick0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
