\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Workers Reach Deal at University of California\b0\par\par\uc2 By Douglas Belkin \par \uc2 331 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 December 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Academic workers at the University of California reached a tentative settlement on Friday, potentially drawing to an end one of the most disruptive work actions in American higher education.\par \par \uc2 If the deal is approved by 36,000 graduate student workers, it would increase minimum pay by about $10,000 to $34,000 for nine months of part-time work, according to a statement from UC President \uc2 Michael Drake\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This is a positive step forward for the University and for our students, and I am grateful for the progress we have made together," said Dr. Drake. "Our Academic Student Employees and Graduate Student Researchers are central to our academic enterprise."\par \par \uc2 Over 2 1/2 years, workers would see raises of up to 66%, according to a statement released by the union.\par \par \uc2 "This is trulya historic win for all the workers who went on strike," said Rafael Jaime, president of \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  Local 2865. "The contract really does submit a new standard for teachers in higher education and we are very proud of [what] we were able to achieve."\par \par \uc2 The strike has lasted 32 days, upending classes at the 10 UC campuses, canceling some lectures and disrupting final exams. In total, 48,000 academic workers walked off their jobs last month. Strikers were represented by the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . Hundreds of faculty supported the strike.\par \par \uc2 Last week, both sides agreed to bring in an independent mediator, \uc2 Darrell Steinberg\uc2 , the mayor of Sacramento and former leader of the state senate. Beyond salary increases, the agreement also includes child care reimbursements.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the bargaining unit representing about a quarter of the strikers reached an agreement with the university. Postdocs will see a salary increase of up to 23% by next fall and $2,500 annual child-care subsidies.\par \par \uc2 The strike was closely watched by colleges and universities across the country as labor unrest among contingent faculty and graduate student employees has simmered.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020221219eicj00030\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
