\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: New York Times Staffers Strike for a Day Over Pact\b0\par\par\uc2 By Alexandra Bruell \par \uc2 597 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 December 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 More than 1,000 New York Times staffers went on strike on Thursday for the first time in over 40 years, its newsroom union said, putting the organization in the position of having to cover news for one day without the majority of its reporters.\par \par \uc2 The one-day work stoppage comes as contract negotiations between management and the members of the NewsGuild, which represents 1,450 Times staffers -- including 1,270 newsroom employees -- have stalled for nearly two years over pay and benefits.\par \par \uc2 Scores of union members picketed outside the entrance to the Times building in Midtown Manhattan Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 "Like all my colleagues, I've watched the value of my salary go down as inflation goes up," said Andy Newman, a Times metro reporter for over 25 years, at the rally. "I really, really love working here, and all I want is to get this settled and get a fair contract."\par \par \uc2 The contract negotiations have centered around pay, retirement and other benefits. The two sides haven't yet come to terms on wages, including the size of raises for the next four years, according to the union and Times management.\par \par \uc2 Many members of the Times newsroom also took to social media to urge people not to use the Times's platforms Thursday, including not playing Wordle, its popular word game.\par \par \uc2 In anticipation of the strike, the Times had identified editors with reporting backgrounds who could cover Thursday's news, according to people familiar with the company.\par \par \uc2 Some stories on the Times's website and app on Thursday simply carried a "by the \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " byline, while others were written by newsroom editors.\par \par \uc2 However, many of the day's biggest news stories -- including the prisoner swap involving basketball star Brittney Griner, as well as the \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2 's decision to sue \uc2 Microsoft Corp\uc2 . to block its planned acquisition of \uc2 Activision Blizzard Inc\uc2 . -- were by traditional beat reporters.\par \par \uc2 "We will produce a robust report on Thursday," Executive Editor \uc2 Joseph Kahn\uc2  wrote in a memo to staff on Wednesday evening. "But it will be harder than usual."\par \par \uc2 More than 1,100 union members have pledged not to work Thursday and forgo pay, a NewsGuild representative said. Taking into account employees who aren't part of the union, the Times has more than 1,800 newsroom staffers around the world.\par \par \uc2 Many strikers outside of the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  building on Thursday were holding noisemakers and homemade signs, and chanted phrases like, "Give us raises, not a lunchbox."\par \par \uc2 In a company memo Wednesday night, Chief Executive \uc2 Meredith Kopit Levien\uc2  said the Times had created hundreds of new journalism jobs in recent years. "At the same time, our ability to carry out our mission is inextricably linked to our financial success as a company," she wrote.\par \par \uc2 The union and management have been in contract talks for 20 months. Both sides were still negotiating on Wednesday afternoon ahead of a union-imposed deadline -- the Times union had said last week it would go on strike Thursday if a contract deal hadn't been reached by then -- but didn't come to an agreement.\par \par \uc2 During the bargaining process, the Times rejected a proposed wage floor of $65,000 for all Guild members, instead offering $62,500 in 2024, according to people familiar with the matter. The company recently offered a choice between keeping a pension plan or selecting a new 401(k) plan, a change from its initial proposal of replacing the pension with the 401(k).\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020221209eic90000j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
89
