\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: U.S. Watch\b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 November 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CALIFORNIA\par \par \uc2 University Workers\par \par \uc2 Walk Off the Job\par \par \uc2 Nearly 50,000 academic workers across the sprawling University of California system walked off the job and onto picket lines Monday, demanding higher wages and better benefits.\par \par \uc2 The teaching assistants, researchers and postdoctoral fellows failed to reach a deal with the university system over the weekend as they demanded pay increases to match the rising cost of housing and inflation. The employees are represented by the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , which called the strike the largest in the history of U.S. higher education.\par \par \uc2 The university system has said its 10 campuses would remain open, but the strike has already caused disruption of some classes just weeks before final exams. Workers on the picket lines are responsible for core aspects of the university including teaching, grading and tutoring.\par \par \uc2 -- Douglas Belkin\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 COVID-19\par \par \uc2 Booster Shows Strong\par \par \uc2 Immune Response\par \par \uc2 Moderna Inc\uc2 .'s new updated Covid-19 booster shot for the U.S. generated strong immune responses in people against Omicron subvariants, according to the first data from a company-sponsored study testing the new doses in volunteers.\par \par \uc2 Moderna\uc2  said on Monday that people receiving the updated booster shot had more than five times the neutralizing antibodies against Omicron subvariants BA.4 and BA.5 than people who received \uc2 Moderna\uc2 's original booster shot.\par \par \uc2 "That really bodes well for the vaccine and public health," \uc2 Moderna\uc2  President \uc2 Stephen Hoge\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Moderna\uc2 's updated booster shot, introduced in the U.S. after regulators authorized it in late August, targets both the original strain of the coronavirus and the BA.4 and BA.5 subvariants, which share an identical surface protein.\par \par \uc2 -- Peter Loftus\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\par \par \uc2 Court Lets Jan. 6 Panel\par \par \uc2 Obtain Phone Records\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court cleared the way Monday for House Jan. 6 investigators to obtain phone records from Arizona Republican Party Chairwoman \uc2 Kelli Ward\uc2 , rejecting her argument that her First Amendment political rights shield her from congressional investigatory powers.\par \par \uc2 In a brief unsigned order, the court denied Ms. Ward's request to stay lower-court decisions upholding the subpoena from the select committee investigating the attack on the U.S. Capitol by supporters of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Justices \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  said they would have granted Ms. Ward's request.\par \par \uc2 The House committee subpoenaed service provider T-Mobile for records from Nov. 1, 2020, to Jan. 31, 2021.\par \par \uc2 During that period, Ms. Ward spoke with Mr. Trump about his efforts to overturn the election.\par \par \uc2 -- Jess Bravin\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020221115eibf0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
