\par\par \b \uc2 When a Union Busts a Union\b0\par\par\uc2 By Michael Saltsman and Charlyce Bozzello \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A17\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  likes to say that "union busting is disgusting" -- but that same union is allegedly union-busting in its negotiations with its own staff.\par \par \uc2 SEIU Local 2015, one of the union's largest chapters in California, represents more than 400,000 healthcare workers. The local has been in a contract battle with its staff, represented by Chapter 15 of the Pacific Northwest Staff Union since 2021. The staff is mainly concerned about wage scales and healthcare costs.\par \par \uc2 After making little progress in negotiations, 95% of the staff voted to authorize a strike this past October. Apparently that threat wasn't enough, and the staff went on strike on Nov. 1, marching in picket lines in Los Angeles and Sacramento. The strike ended on Sunday, with a public statement that declared a "culture of toxicity" at Local 2015.\par \par \uc2 According to Local 2015 organizer Alex Sanchez, \uc2 SEIU\uc2  management tried to intimidate workers on the picket line, becoming antagonistic. Far from showing union solidarity with its unionized staff, the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  apparently took union-busting a bit too literally. The \uc2 SEIU\uc2 's human-resources manager had a hit-and-run charge filed against her after she was seen driving her pickup truck into Mr. Sanchez on the picket line. According to Mr. Sanchez, other vehicles driven by \uc2 SEIU\uc2  management have "aggressively crept" through the throng of picketers.\par \par \uc2 There also are allegations that \uc2 SEIU\uc2  managers recorded the protest, a potential violation under the National Labor Relations Act. An email from \uc2 SEIU\uc2  management to staff was seen as an attempt to get workers to become scabs, crossing the picket line. The union also listed several job postings on UnionJobs.com, which was interpreted by the striking staff as an attempt to replace them.\par \par \uc2 According to PNWSU, this union staff strike is one of the largest in history, spreading down California from Oakland to San Bernardino.\par \par \uc2 But it's not the first time the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  has faced criticism from its own staff. In 2019 staff at the union's Washington headquarters accused the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  of union-busting behavior. According to staffers, the \uc2 SEIU\uc2  had been outsourcing union jobs, eliminating work for staff members and misclassifying employees. Staff even hung a banner outside the union headquarters that said "Stop Union Busting." Staff members represented by Office and Professional Employees International Union Local 2 begged union managers to "practice what they preach."\par \par \uc2 Apparently, the lesson didn't sink in. \uc2 SEIU\uc2  management claims it is "committed to bargaining in good faith" and listening to workers' concerns. But the union has been quick to call out private companies, including the coffee giant \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , that participate in similar back-and-forth negotiations. Union-friendly baristas regularly take to \uc2 Twitter\uc2  to criticize \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  management for milder tactics than those the union's own management has engaged in.\par \par \uc2 Labor unions are employers too. And they don't mind flipping the script when it's their own staff at the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Mr. Saltsman is managing director at the Employment Policies Institute. Ms. Bozzello is communications director at the Center for Union Facts.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020221114eibe0001n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
