\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. News: Seattle Teachers Vote to End Weeklong Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ben Chapman \par \uc2 314 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Teachers in Seattle voted Tuesday night to end a strike that delayed the start of the school year for a week for Washington's largest district.\par \par \uc2 The Seattle Education Association, which represents about 6,000 teachers and classroom aides, authorized the strike Sept. 6 after failing to reach an agreement with Seattle Public Schools over conditions and pay.\par \par \uc2 Classes were supposed to start the following day, but the district called off school for its roughly 50,000 students after the union prepared for a work stoppage and established picket lines around the city.\par \par \uc2 District officials on Monday reached a tentative agreement with union leadership on a contract for teachers after negotiations.\par \par \uc2 Seattle Public Schools officials said the district would begin classes Wednesday. "This was an incredible effort by both teams and we put the needs of our students first," Superintendent Brent Jones said Tuesday in a video message to families.\par \par \uc2 The district didn't release the details of the tentative deal.\par \par \uc2 Seattle Education Association officials said the union sought better support for students affected by the pandemic, including more counselors on school campuses. The union also sought smaller classes and more teachers.\par \par \uc2 Union officials on Tuesday said in a statement they had "won a great tentative agreement and started an important conversation with our community about supporting our students." Members will vote to approve the agreement this week, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 As schools across the country this year face labor shortages, a few other unions at universities and school districts across the country have initiated strikes.\par \par \uc2 Faculty members at \uc2 Eastern Michigan University\uc2  on Sunday ended a strike that began Sept. 7 after the professors' union reached a pact with the administration. The teachers union in Columbus, Ohio, last month went on a three-day strike before reaching a contract deal.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220914ei9e0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
