\par\par \b \uc2 Railroads Plan Curb On Freight As Strike Measure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Esther Fung and Paul Berger \par \uc2 554 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 September 2022\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Freight railroads said they are planning to halt the transport of hazardous materials and sensitive cargoes, such as chemicals used in fertilizer and chlorine for water purification, as they continue negotiations with two labor unions.\par \par \uc2 Railroads have informed customers that they may stop accepting certain types of freight, including bulk shipments, to avoid materials being unattended or unsecured in case of a work stoppage. Rail customers such as agricultural companies are evaluating contingency plans, including shutting down processing plants amid rail delays, or hiring alternative transportation providers such as trucking companies.\par \par \uc2 The ripple effects of the railroads' plans are extending beyond freight traffic. \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  said it would begin reducing some passenger services Tuesday by canceling trips over three long-distance routes.\par \par \uc2 The freight railroads have already reached new labor deals or are completing tentative agreements with 10 unions, and are in continuing talks with two groups representing about 66,000 workers. The two remaining unions, the \uc2 Brotherhood of Locomotive Engineers and Trainmen\uc2 , and SMART-Transportation Division, said Sunday that the railroads' plans to restrict cargo is a move to "extort a contract settlement" and that they remain at the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 The talks involving railroad labor groups and companies including Norfolk Southern Corp. and Union Pacific Corp. have been going on for months.\par \par \uc2 A White House-appointed panel has already interceded with recommendations for a deal ahead of a Friday deadline for an agreement.\par \par \uc2 If those negotiations remain at a stalemate, workers for two unions representing rail engineers and other employees could decide to stop work. Both groups voted to authorize a strike if a deal isn't reached.\par \par \uc2 President Biden in July appointed a federal panel to help resolve the railroad labor dispute, a move that opened a 60-day window for mediation. That period ends this week.\par \par \uc2 Labor Secretary \uc2 Marty Walsh\uc2  on Sunday pushed the unions and their employers to reach an agreement to avoid a rail shutdown, said a representative from the Labor Department. The National Economic Council has also held meetings about railroad labor negotiations, and Mr. Biden has been briefed about the progress of negotiations, according to White House officials.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the president made calls to union representatives and rail companies in a bid to avert a strike, one of the White House officials said.\par \par \uc2 "The fact that we are already seeing some impacts of contingency planning by railways again demonstrates that a shutdown of our freight rail system is an unacceptable outcome for our economy and the American people, and all parties must work to avoid that," the Labor Department representative said.\par \par \uc2 Labor negotiations are also being closely watched by rail customers and business groups amid broader concerns that a prolonged dispute could upend supply chains.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Chamber of Commerce\uc2 , in a letter to congressional leaders Monday, said the restriction on hazardous materials "threatens to send equity and commodity markets spiraling." It warned that a full rail shutdown could cost the U.S. economy $2 billion a day.\par \par \uc2 Amtrak\uc2  relies on freight railroads for almost all of its intercity routes outside of the Northeast Corridor, and wants to avoid the risk of passenger trains getting trapped in the disruptions, a spokesman said.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Andrew Restuccia and Patrick Thomas contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020220913ei9d0001q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
